WEBVTT

00:04:28.806 --> 00:04:31.559
“Sippin’ on gin and juice, laid back,

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.227
with my mind on my money

00:04:33.227 --> 00:04:34.895
and my money on my mind."

00:04:35.229 --> 00:04:38.941
In the song, Snoop references
a brand of gin called Seagram's,

00:04:38.941 --> 00:04:40.985
and the success of the song
"Gin and Juice"

00:04:41.027 --> 00:04:44.280
led to a roughly 20 percent increase
in Seagram's gin sales.

00:04:44.947 --> 00:04:46.157
Now you may be thinking,

00:04:46.157 --> 00:04:48.826
"Alright, Samir, I see the point
you're trying to make,

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:51.329
but using hip hop to sell alcohol is easy.

00:04:51.704 --> 00:04:53.998
Climate change is a little bit
more complex."

00:04:54.498 --> 00:04:55.708
Fair enough.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.209
But there are examples

00:04:57.251 --> 00:05:00.379
of how hip hop artists have leveraged
their cultural capital